.TH "setup-lb-addressing" "8" "2026-09-11" "ltsp6"
.SH "NAME"
setup\-lb\-addressing \(em Give the keepalived pair static addresses and matching peers
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
\fBsetup\-lb\-addressing\fR \fIown\-ip/cidr\fR \fIpeer\-ip\fR \fIiface\fR \fIgateway\fR \fIdns\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Run on each load balancer, as root. Sets the static address and rewrites
\fBunicast_src_ip\fR and \fBunicast_peer\fR in keepalived.conf to match, then
reboots onto the new configuration.
.PP
Run it before deploying haproxy\-rdp.cfg. Everything else on these two hosts
names a peer by address, and an address that moves takes the pair apart.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
.IP "\fIown\-ip/cidr\fP" 4
This node's static address.
.IP "\fIpeer\-ip\fP" 4
The other node's static address, written into \fBunicast_peer\fR.
.IP "\fIiface\fP \fIgateway\fP \fIdns\fP" 4
Interface, default gateway and resolver.
.SH "EXAMPLE"
.PP
.nf
setup\-lb\-addressing 172.17.250.51/20 172.17.250.52 ens18 \
    172.17.240.1 172.17.250.10      # on lb1
setup\-lb\-addressing 172.17.250.52/20 172.17.250.51 ens18 \
    172.17.240.1 172.17.250.10      # on lb2
.fi
.SH "NOTES"
.PP
keepalived announces over unicast here because a virtual switch does not relay
VRRP multicast between guests. Unicast works \(em but it names each peer by
address, and both nodes were on DHCP. When the leases changed, neither node saw
the other's advertisements, both promoted themselves to MASTER, and both
answered ARP for the VIP. Connections were established through one node while
their follow\-up packets arrived at the other, which reset them: RDP sessions
died five to nine seconds in, HAProxy logging the abort in the data phase
(\fBCD\fR), while the session server showed the session running happily.
.PP
Check that exactly one node holds the addresses:
.PP
.nf
ip \-4 \-o addr show | grep \-E '172\.17\.249\.22[23]'
.fi
.PP
The same failure had already taken out the Corosync quorum earlier, in a
different disguise. \fBAny configuration that names a peer by address needs
that address to be static\fR \(em and on a hypervisor whose virtual switch
re\-randomises its subnet on host reboot, that includes checking the subnet
itself has not moved.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
